WEBVTT

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.050
[Grimmel] When all is said and done,

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:12.512
this young chief
will bring me the Night Fury.

00:00:13.596 --> 00:00:18.100
They don't have a leader, just a boy.

00:00:20.811 --> 00:00:21.896
[Stoick] Hiccup.

00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:27.235
This is Berk, son.

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:29.987
It's our home.

00:00:31.572 --> 00:00:35.826
It was the home of your grandparents
and their grandparents before them.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.247
And it's my job as chief
to protect us, Hiccup.

00:00:39.997 --> 00:00:44.835
And one day, when you're all grown up,
that job will be passed on to you.

00:00:44.919 --> 00:00:46.170
[Hiccup] Okay.

00:00:46.254 --> 00:00:51.133
And it's very important, son,
because out there, beyond the sunset,

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:54.262
lies the home of the dragons.

00:00:54.971 --> 00:00:55.972
Wow!

00:00:56.055 --> 00:01:00.643
Aye! Legends tell of ships
that sailed too close to it,

00:01:00.726 --> 00:01:04.981
only to drop off the edge of the world,
never to be seen again.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:06.190
[gasps]

00:01:06.274 --> 00:01:11.237
But those sailors who turned back
told tales of a great waterfall

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:14.699
and dragons guarding the entrance
to a Hidden World.

00:01:14.949 --> 00:01:17.285
-Whoa.
-Not just a nest, Hiccup,

00:01:18.119 --> 00:01:20.955
but a land from which all dragons come.

00:01:21.455 --> 00:01:24.041
Even Night Furies?

00:01:24.208 --> 00:01:26.294
[chuckles] Especially Night Furies.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.713
[shudders] Those are scary.

00:01:28.796 --> 00:01:29.755
Don't you worry.

00:01:30.339 --> 00:01:33.968
One day I'll find the Hidden World
and seal it up...

00:01:35.052 --> 00:01:39.140
so that people and dragons
will fight no more.

00:01:43.227 --> 00:01:45.605
[dragons calling]

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.609
[grunts]

00:01:49.692 --> 00:01:50.693
What?

00:01:51.152 --> 00:01:52.570
[grunts pleadingly]

00:01:52.653 --> 00:01:53.905
Oh, all right.

00:01:53.988 --> 00:01:56.282
You do know
it's not a chew toy, don't you?

00:01:56.365 --> 00:01:58.576
Is this what you want?
Oh, do you want this leg?

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:01.078
Do you want my leg? [grunts] Go get it.

00:02:10.922 --> 00:02:12.882
[Toothless grunting happily]

00:02:12.965 --> 00:02:15.217
Getting pretty good
at gliding on your own, bud.

00:02:18.346 --> 00:02:19.513
[pants]

00:02:19.889 --> 00:02:21.933
[grunting softly]

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:27.146
[squawks]

00:02:28.397 --> 00:02:29.523
Oh!

00:02:29.607 --> 00:02:32.485
So this is where you come
to get away from Gobber.

00:02:32.568 --> 00:02:34.987
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:02:37.073 --> 00:02:38.157
Ugh!

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.575
[Stormfly squawks]

00:02:40.076 --> 00:02:41.577
Well, he's right, you know.

00:02:41.744 --> 00:02:44.997
[stammers] Really?
You think you and I should...

00:02:45.081 --> 00:02:48.292
Oh, gods, no.
We're nowhere near ready for that.

00:02:48.876 --> 00:02:50.378
No, that's... That's crazy.

00:02:50.461 --> 00:02:52.630
I mean, he's right about all of this.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:57.259
[sighs] It does seem
like the whole world knows about us now.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.929
Yep. And the more dragons
we bring back here,

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:01.847
the bigger of a target we become.

00:03:02.431 --> 00:03:03.432
Ugh!

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:07.019
I just wish there was some way
to make them leave us alone.

00:03:07.895 --> 00:03:09.105
There might be.

00:03:11.816 --> 00:03:14.443
Dad used to talk
about an old mariners' myth

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.029
of a secret land at the edge of the world,

00:03:17.113 --> 00:03:19.281
where dragons live totally out of reach.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:23.285
[chuckles] Well, sailors
are known for tall tales.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.370
True.

00:03:24.745 --> 00:03:26.038
But what if it's real?

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:29.208
It could be the answer
to all of our problems.

00:03:29.291 --> 00:03:30.292
How?

00:03:30.793 --> 00:03:32.837
By moving the dragons there?

00:03:33.504 --> 00:03:35.548
Uh-uh. All of us.

00:03:35.923 --> 00:03:36.924
Seriously?

00:03:37.675 --> 00:03:40.553
And abandon our home of seven generations?

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.848
-The home your father left you to protect.
-[sighs]

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:46.767
-Uh...
-Yeah, I think we need

00:03:46.851 --> 00:03:48.144
a real solution, Hiccup.

00:03:48.519 --> 00:03:49.645
[Stormfly squeals]

00:03:50.521 --> 00:03:51.897
[growls]

00:03:52.773 --> 00:03:53.816
[chitters]

00:03:53.983 --> 00:03:57.028
Well, we could just take Gobber's advice
and tie the knot.

00:03:57.111 --> 00:03:58.529
That should fix everything.

00:03:59.113 --> 00:04:02.074
But, hey, if you're having doubts
about yours truly,

00:04:02.158 --> 00:04:04.452
I'm pretty sure Snotlout's available.

00:04:04.535 --> 00:04:06.662
[chuckles] He only has eyes for your mom.

00:04:06.829 --> 00:04:09.081
[gasps] Oh!

00:04:09.165 --> 00:04:10.666
Playing dirty now, huh?

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:11.876
[chuckles] You asked for it.

00:04:11.959 --> 00:04:14.462
Looks like there might be
a wedding after all.

00:04:14.545 --> 00:04:17.590
-Oh, how dare you? That is a low blow.
-[giggles]

00:04:17.673 --> 00:04:19.800
No, no, you are not getting away.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.928
[groans] Okay, okay, you win, you win.

00:04:23.012 --> 00:04:24.346
You always win.

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:26.849
You knew what you were getting into.

00:04:26.932 --> 00:04:28.934
-Uh-huh. Right.
-[dragon calling in distance]

00:04:35.316 --> 00:04:36.650
Uh, bud?

00:04:40.738 --> 00:04:43.115
What... Yeah, sure,
don't bother to wait for us.

00:04:43.741 --> 00:04:44.742
[sighs]

00:04:47.703 --> 00:04:48.954
[sniffing]

00:04:56.128 --> 00:04:57.963
[dragon calling in distance]

00:05:03.177 --> 00:05:04.762
[continues sniffing]

00:05:21.195 --> 00:05:22.404
[growls softly]

00:05:27.743 --> 00:05:29.745
[purring softly]

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:42.299
[grunts softly]

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.181
[squawks]

00:05:49.306 --> 00:05:50.391
[grunts]

00:05:52.017 --> 00:05:53.561
[growls and hisses]

00:05:54.645 --> 00:05:55.479
[grunts]

00:05:56.021 --> 00:05:57.648
[sniffing]

00:06:04.071 --> 00:06:05.322
[shudders]

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:17.459
[both grunting softly]

00:06:23.591 --> 00:06:25.676
-[twig snaps in distance]
-[snarls]

00:06:26.844 --> 00:06:28.012
[Astrid screams]

00:06:29.221 --> 00:06:30.431
[growls softly]

00:06:36.353 --> 00:06:37.771
Oh, my gods!

00:06:37.938 --> 00:06:40.316
-[yowls]
-Uh, Hiccup!

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:41.692
[both groan]

00:06:42.693 --> 00:06:43.861
[snarls]

00:06:43.944 --> 00:06:45.154
[growls]

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:48.115
Yeah, yeah, we're...
We're friends. No need to kill us.

00:06:48.449 --> 00:06:49.533
[growls]

00:06:49.992 --> 00:06:52.453
-[screeching softly]
-[roars]

